.TH PLUGIN-QUALIFY-RECORDS-PACKAGE 1 "October 2026" "plugin-qualify" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plugin-qualify-records-package \- the Debian package of a device's qualification records
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plugin-qualify-records-package
.I qualification-dir
\fB\-\-host\-class\fR \fIclass\fR \fB\-\-set\fR \fIset\fR \fB\-\-provenance\fR \fIjson\fR
[\fB\-\-version\fR \fIversion\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-maintainer\fR \fIwho\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Builds \fBomx-qualification-\fIclass\fB-\fIset\fB_\fIversion\fB_all.deb\fR from the qualification directory
plugin-qualify-sync(1) left on a device. The package installs every record, with the probe output it judged, under
/usr/share/omx/qualification/\fIclass\fR/\fIset\fR/ beside \fBprovenance.json\fR, and depends on the
plugin-qualify that reads that directory. On another device of the class, plugin-qualify-sync takes a plugin from
those records instead of measuring it, and only when every file of the installed plugin hashes as the measured one
did.
.PP
A record whose probe output is missing, or is not the copy it names, is left out and named on standard error; so is
an unmeasured record, which never applies. The last line on standard output names the package, its records and its
files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-host\-class " class"
The machine class the records were measured on (\fBrpi5\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-set " set"
The plugin set they cover (\fBzynthian-vangelis\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-provenance " json"
A JSON file, or the JSON itself, with what the tool cannot know: the image, the package versions and the source
revisions of the device. The set, the class, the package and the date are added.
.TP
.BI \-\-version " version"
The package's version; the default is the build date, \fB2026.10.29\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " dir"
Where the package is written (default: the current directory).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 the package was written; 2 it could not be.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR plugin-qualify-sync (1)
